{#
  Bill Pay — Scene gallery. Figma: node 856:9399 ("section" instance),
  Portfolio file (3XG9JnADI2psNR3B7TwQdx). Replaces the earlier accordion-list
  version (_includes/accordion-gallery.njk) in the last section of the Bill
  Pay case study — that file is superseded and left in place unreferenced,
  not deleted.

  Layout shell: iframe stage (800x452, mock renders at 650 centered — the
  remaining 150px of width is clearance for the row-lift-out scene
  animation's overhang, up to 65px per side) + navigation (caption + the
  shared gallery controls from gallery-navigation.njk), 650 wide to match.
  Scene 1's content and animation live in
  assets/scene-gallery/bill-pay/scenes.html; scenes 2/3 are still
  placeholders.

  Standalone component — no section wrapper, no headline, no background.
  Caller drops {{ sceneGallery() }} into its own content column.
#}
{% from "gallery-navigation.njk" import galleryInteraction %}

{% macro sceneGallery() %}
<div class="scene-gallery">
  <div class="scene-gallery__stage">
    <iframe class="scene-gallery__visual" id="scene-gallery-visual" title="Bill Pay scene"></iframe>
  </div>
  <div class="scene-gallery__navigation">
    <div class="scene-gallery__caption" id="scene-gallery-caption">
      <img class="scene-gallery__icon" src="../../assets/illustrations/bill-pay/volume-productivity.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
      <div class="scene-gallery__caption-column" id="scene-gallery-caption-column">
        <p class="scene-gallery__headline" id="scene-gallery-headline"><span class="scene-gallery__headline-strong"># Volume_Productivity</span> | <span class="scene-gallery__headline-variant" id="scene-gallery-headline-variant"></span></p>
        <p class="scene-gallery__description" id="scene-gallery-description"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {{ galleryInteraction("scene-gallery") }}
  </div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
